{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>the edge of it.</b> Only the edge of it." "<b>וקבנו.</b> A strange word. According to grammar the imperative is like the future, and there is no difference between them except the sign: ירדפהו / ירדפנו / ירדפוהו / אויב ירדפו. This word comes compounded with nun and with cholam. According to the opinion of Rabbi Judah the first grammarian, that it is from the root קבן, if so it cannot be an imperative, for such is found in the binyan kal. Perhaps it is a verbal noun on the pattern of ומשמרו את השבועה."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra's grammatical argument is compressed and elliptical; rendered literally without expanding the implied reasoning."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:08.189410442Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}